 "review": {
  "management_type_reason": "stauden.de・品種: 咲き終わった花茎を株元の葉まで切る（試作のホスタ 'Gold Standard' と同じ線引き）。RHS は傷んだ葉の除去と秋の枯れ葉の片付けのみ。花後の根拠は stauden.de の1件だけ。機械の A から変更",
  "management_type_quote": "Rückschnitt abgeblühter Stängel bis zum grundständigen Blattschopf",
  "management_type_by_matching": "A 放任型",
  "heat_west_only": "中",
  "muggy_west_only": null,
  "heat_muggy_west_evidence": "[NC State/属] In the south it is best to plant hosta in full shade or dappled shade so that the foliage colors will be more vibrant and won't develop leaf burn.\n[NC State/属] Hosta plantaginea  originated in China and is very fragrant and tolerates heat.\n[RHS/品種] Aspect: North-facing or East-facing（西向き・南向きが入っていない）",
  "spread_evidence": "[地下茎 2／MBG・品種] Stalked, conspicuously-veined, often dense, basal leaves in a variety of shapes, sizes, colors and textures rise up from a central rhizomatous crown to form a rounded to spreading mound of foliage.\n[増え方] こぼれ種・地下茎の段階に合わせて直した（前：株立ち）",
